  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "The BODMAS rule is given as-\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/0b7a0ec72c26c83c63bdfe961e28fc0a0c2e2f4f4f159e1c1ecb1c0845ca3e70.png] \n\nThe logic followed here is:\n\n 'A' means '+' , 'B' means '×' and C means '-'.\n\nFrom 16 A 13 B 6 C 9 = 85, we get-\n\n→ 16 + __**13 × 6**__ - 9 = 85\n\n→ __**16 + 78**__ - 9 = 85\n\n→ __**94 - 9**__ = 85\n\n→ 85 = 85\n\nFrom 15 A 20 B 7 C 30 = 125, we get-\n\n→ 15 + __**20**____** __**__× 7__ - 30 = 125\n\n→ __**15 + 140**__ - 30 = 125\n\n→ __**155 - 30**__ = 125\n\n→ 125 = 125\n\nSo, 'A' means '+' , 'B' means '×' and C means '-'.\n\nSimilarly for 10 A 15 B 6 C 20 = ?, we get-\n\n→ 10 + **__15__****__ __**__× 6__ - 20 = ?\n\n→ __**10 + 90**__ - 20 = ?\n\n→ __**100 - 20**__ = ?\n\n→ 80 = 80\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".",
